course: dictionary
lesson: 13145
title: Forenoon: an old word for morning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Forenoon is an old-fashioned word for the morning, the time before midday. You will meet it in old books, in ships' logs and in some formal writing. Today most people say morning instead.
explain: Look at the word in two parts: fore means before, and noon means midday. Put them together and you get the time before noon. Looking for small words inside a long word is a good clue when you meet something new.
explain: «We went to the park in the forenoon, before lunch.» The words before lunch are a clue. Lunch comes after midday, so forenoon must be the time before it. Swap in morning: «We went to the park in the morning, before lunch.» It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
fact: Forenoon means the morning, the time before midday.
fact: Fore means before, and noon means midday, so forenoon means before noon.
fact: In time problems, the forenoon is the hours before 12 noon, which we also write as a.m.
fact: «In the forenoon» means in the morning, and you may see «the forenoon watch» in old ships' logs.
fact: Old and formal words like forenoon are not wrong; they belong to older books, formal writing and some Scottish use.
exercise: «The baker sells bread in the forenoon and cakes in the afternoon.» What does forenoon mean? | The time after lunch | *The morning, before midday | The middle of the night | The evening, after dark
exercise: What does fore mean in the word forenoon? | *Before | Above | Again | Under
exercise: «We cleaned the boat all forenoon, then had lunch.» Which time is the forenoon? | The middle of the night | *The hours before midday | The hours after lunch | The hours after dark
test: Forenoon is another word for | Teatime | *Morning | Evening | Midnight
test: Which phrase means in the morning? | After tea | *In the forenoon | At bedtime | Late at night
exam: Which is correct? | Forenoon means midnight | *Forenoon means the time before midday | Forenoon means the evening | Forenoon means the time after midday
